  "worked_solution": "First, notice that $3!=3\\cdot 2!$ and $5!=5\\cdot 4!\\,.$ Then, we can cancel the $2!$ and $4!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3!\\,4!}{5!\\,2!} & =\\frac{3\\cdot 2!\\cdot 4!}{5\\cdot 4!\\,\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot \\cancel{2!\\,}\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{5\\cdot \\cancel{4!\\,}\\cdot \\cancel{2!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
